gemma2b_it_fewshot3:
`Memoization` is a technique to store the results of function calls and return them next time the same inputs occur. In this example, `fib(n)` function is memoized by storing the results in a dictionary. The first call to `fib(5)` will take longer than the subsequent calls, as the result is computed and stored.

```javascript
const fibCache = new Object();

function fib(n) {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  if (fibCache[n]) return fibCache[n];
  return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
}

console.log(fib(5)); // 5
console.log(fib(5)); // 8
```

